cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TardigradeDB in academic or industry research, please cite it as below."
title: "TardigradeDB: A KV-cache-native persistent memory engine for large language models"
abstract: >-
  TardigradeDB is a from-scratch Rust + PyO3 memory engine that stores
  the Key-Value cache tensors of large language models directly,
  retrieves them via attention-native scoring in latent space, and
  injects them back into the model without consuming prompt tokens.
  It treats memory as a managed OS resource via a four-layer
  architecture (Storage, Retrieval, Organization, Governance) with
  adaptive lifecycle policies, crash-safe persistence, and per-owner
  isolation.
type: software
version: "0.8.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
license: MIT
